{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Release lock-in over code and drafted notes (Gawande, Minto, Raskin)","verdict":"pass","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"advisory","summary":"The debug note blurs an unparseable resolution with other unparseable record fields. The code routes an unknown resolution on a forced-risk record to the interrupt path, but an unparseable risk declaration can route to repair-risk-declaration; a resolved record that is not continued stays prior memory even when its handoff is invalid.","evidence":["The notes say “unresolved or unparseable records still force the interrupt route.”","debug_artifact_state.py routes unreadable risk declarations with reason risk-declaration-unreadable.","test_debug_plan.py::test_resolved_unparseable_risk_declaration_is_not_demoted expects a bare invalid risk declaration to route to repair-risk-declaration.","test_debug_plan.py::test_resolved_forced_risk_without_allowed_matching_handoff_is_prior_memory_when_not_continued covers invalid handoffs on resolved, noncontinued records. "],"action":"Clarify that unresolved or unknown resolution on a forced-risk record keeps the interrupt route; distinguish malformed risk declarations and resolved prior records."},{"id":"F2","severity":"advisory","summary":"The Node mutation-reporter warning and older-Node workaround are not independently substantiated by the bound inputs. The specific test, observed reporter output, and Node version are not included.","evidence":["The drafted notes describe a `node --test` reporter failure and recommend an older Node major on PATH.","The bound v8.14.7 quality receipt records a pass but does not identify the Node version or include the failure evidence."],"action":"Retain this operator guidance only if the failure and workaround are confirmed by a focused repro; otherwise remove or qualify it."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Codex resume behavior lacks a live-host invocation in the bound evidence.","bin":"non-blocking","disposition":"The fake-executor test explicitly bounds its claim to invocation construction and verifies the original model and effort options survive resume; no live-host result is claimed here."},{"concern":"The linked-worktree promotion fix has only unit-level evidence.","bin":"not a concern","disposition":"The bound tests exercise a real Git linked worktree, repeated promotion, cleanup, and collision handling."},{"concern":"The implementation-lane stop refinement lacks an end-to-end model behavior test.","bin":"non-blocking","disposition":"The change is prompt shaping; the source carries the revised directions and tests pin their presence. The notes describe that policy."}],"next_move":"The four fix summaries are supported by their bound source and tests. Clarify the debug routing wording and confirm or qualify the carried Node issue before publication; version, manifest, and claims-review surfaces remain for the separate review.","non_claims":["No tests or live Codex/Muse host invocations were run; this review relies on the bound source and test content.","The generated derived-claim, version, manifest, and claims-review surfaces were not judged in this review."]}
